    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d14">

                <pb facs="0040" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 FEAC/1–1349</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State for Occupied Areas</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Saltzman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        United States Representative on the Far Eastern Commission</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McCoy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-25">January 25,
                        1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General McCoy</hi>: With your letter of January
                    13, 1949 to the Secretary of State,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d14-f1"/> you forwarded
                    a request by the Far Eastern Commission for consultation with the Supreme
                    Commander for the Allied Powers relative to the review of the Japanese
                    Constitution. This request was transmitted to the Supreme Commander who has now
                    replied. I enclose copies of his reply for the information of the
                    Commission.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Saltzman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d14-a1.xml" xpointer="d14-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
